Technology.detail:
Generative AI argues that Respect for artists means not using generative AI. Generative AI dramatically changes societies. AI Usefulness argues that AI-generated code is unreliable. AI threatens professional writers. AI-generated code is unavoidable in game development.

@phoebebarton.bsky.social: “beyond which, we didn't even need modern generative AI in order to produce fucked-up translations. pre-2022 machine translation was perfectly capable of that already”

Generative AI (81.2%) says Generative AI is problematic. AI Usefulness (18.8%) says AI has limited genuine use cases.

AI Not Worth It argues that AI is not worth the cost. AI Value argues that AI has limited value.

@eyepatchguy.bsky.social: “My stance has always been “this thing has potential use cases, but they are not worth the cost as it stands and any serious regulation of AI has to get rid of daily personal use for bullshit reasons or it is meaningless.” I have not changed this position”

AI Not Worth It (73.3%) says AI is not worth the cost. AI Value (26.7%) says AI has limited value.

